==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|satiatus}}, pp. of {{term|satiare||to fill full, satiate}} < {{term|sat}}, {{term|satis||sufficient}}, {{term|satur||full}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-satiate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|satiat|ing}}

# {{transitive}} To [[fill]] to [[satisfaction]]; to [[satisfy]].
#: ''Nothing seemed to '''satiate''' her desire for knowledge.''
# {{transitive}} To [[satisfy]] to [[excess]].

